 "Stop over-looping a phrase. Play a musical idea (e.g. a 4-bar chord progression with melody) once to spark interest and a second time to reinforce it so the listener can remember it. On the third pass, never repeat it unchanged: option 1, go somewhere different (a new melody over the same chords, or a new progression with a new melody); option 2, start the third pass the same and diverge partway (around halfway through the phrase). Choose the option by intent (the response you want from the listener). Use as a check across a loop-based arrangement.",
 ["A written musical idea (e.g. 4-bar chords + melody) in a DAW or sequencer"],
